  "verbalization": "Sabinene is implicated in the inhibition of DNA polymerase iota through a multi-step mechanism involving the target enzyme ME-180 and its derivatives. The evidence suggests that Sabinene acts as a target of ME-180, which in turn is a target of Neopyrrolomycin D and (-)-gamma-Cadinene. These compounds are all known to interact with DNA polymerase iota, indicating a potential pathway where Sabinene may exert its effect through these intermediates. The high scores in the visible paths suggest a strong, consistent relationship between Sabinene and DNA polymerase iota, likely through a direct or indirect interaction at the enzyme level. The presence of multiple pathways converging on DNA polymerase iota supports the hypothesis that Sabinene may modulate its activity, possibly by inhibiting the enzyme or affecting its regulatory processes. The integration of these pathways highlights the complexity of the interaction network, with Sabinene potentially playing a role in the inhibition of DNA polymerase iota through the intermediates listed.",
